---
title: Tuna Pasta
servings: 1
course: dinner
tags: quick, one-pan, pasta, fish
image: https://img.youtube.com/vi/M-PuGg7Ek-w/maxresdefault.jpg
source: https://youtu.be/M-PuGg7Ek-w
time: 15m
---

Fill a large stainless steel #frying pan{} one-third to half full with @water. Bring it to a simmer over high heat, season generously with @salt, and add @spaghetti{100%g}. Cook the pasta until al dente, stirring occasionally so it relaxes into the shallow water.

While the pasta cooks, finely slice the @red chilli{0.5} and finely slice the peeled @garlic{1%clove}. Roughly chop the @flat-leaf parsley{1%handful}.

Once the pasta is al dente, use #tongs{} to transfer it directly onto a serving #plate{} to keep warm, leaving it slightly wet so it does not stick. Pour about half of the starchy cooking water into a #bowl{} to reserve, then discard the rest from the pan.

Return the empty #frying pan{} to medium-high heat and add @extra virgin olive oil{2%tbsp}. Add the sliced garlic and red chilli, sautéing for ~{30%seconds} until fragrant.

Partially drain the @canned tuna in olive oil{1%can} and add the tuna to the pan, breaking it into large chunks. Season with a small pinch of @&salt and add an extra drizzle of @&extra virgin olive oil{1%tbsp}.

Transfer the cooked pasta back into the pan using #tongs{}. Add @caper{1%tbsp} and pour in about 60 ml of the reserved starchy @&water{60%ml}. Toss and stir vigorously to emulsify the olive oil and pasta water into a creamy sauce.

Remove from the heat. Use a #grater{} to grate the zest of @lemon{1} over the pasta, then squeeze in roughly one tablespoon of lemon juice. Toss through the chopped flat-leaf parsley.

Transfer the pasta to the serving #plate{} using #tongs{}, scraping all of the remaining tuna, capers, chilli, and pan sauce over the top. Serve immediately.
